# Patterns here are matched against the whole path from the build context root,
# so a bare `dist` excludes only `/dist` and leaves every `packages/*/dist`
# behind. That is not a tidiness detail: it silently copied a developer's own
# build output into the image, so `npm run build` inside the container found
# everything already present and could not fail. A build-order bug that broke
# every deploy for a day therefore passed locally every time it was tested.
#
# Keep the `**/` on anything that can appear inside a workspace. The container
# must build from source alone, exactly as a fresh clone does.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/build
**/coverage
**/.vite
**/*.tsbuildinfo
storage
backups
# The WhatsApp bridge runs on the office Mac, never in the container: it holds
# long-lived sessions that a restart would break, and its Baileys dependency has
# no business in the deployed image. Excluded so `COPY . .` cannot drag it in.
wa-bridge
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.git
*.log
.DS_Store
